    "summary": "The column of Horns in Isfahan; single-page drawing on an album folio. Column is erected from an octagonal-shaped fort, which stands at the intersecting point of two walls (the left drawn with doors evenly spaced between each column, and the right displaying a single door). Album contains 44 paintings and drawings, mostly of Persian costumes and animals with some drawings by Kaempfer.\r\nInk on paper. Album bound in brown leather with gold gilt decoration. Inside covers have marbled paper.",
